issue.description:
Refine the compact data-table composition so checkbox borders use the semantic input token and Amount values use Sans/Body typography instead of Mono.

Owner direction:

* Lighten the visual weight of the table checkboxes by using the existing semantic input color token for their unchecked border treatment.
* Change the Amount column values from Mono typography to Sans/Body typography.

Checkbox styling:

* Unchecked checkbox border should use the semantic input token, e.g. border-input or the equivalent accepted token mapping.
* Preserve checked and indeterminate states.
* Preserve focus-visible/ring behavior.
* Do not change checkbox size, column width, or selection behavior unless required for the token correction.
* Apply consistently to the header/select-all checkbox and row checkboxes.

Amount typography:

* Amount values such as $316.00 / $242.00 / $837.00 / $874.00 / $721.00 should use Sans/Body typography.
* Remove any Mono/type-mono class or equivalent from the Amount cells.
* Keep numeric alignment/readability intact.
* Do not change the Amount column values or formatting.

Preserve:

* current Table structure;
* Status / Email / Amount columns;
* checkbox column;
* blank row-action header;
* row ellipsis actions;
* semantic borders/dividers;
* light/dark behavior;
* responsive containment;
* accessibility.

Do not:

* change table padding/layout;
* change Status or Email typography;
* add new tokens or public resources;
* alter checkbox semantics;
* change unrelated gallery compositions.

Acceptance:

* Unchecked header and row checkbox borders use the semantic input token and no longer appear overly dark.
* Checked/indeterminate/focus states still work correctly.
* Amount values render with Sans/Body typography rather than Mono.
* Amount formatting and alignment remain correct.
* No accessibility, keyboard, focus, responsive, or theme regression.
